 "segments": [
  {
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 3.38,
   "text": "Someone looks at you in the street and they say Alex, what idea should I pursue? I've just quit my job."
  },
  {
   "s": 4.22,
   "e": 7.82,
   "text": "So I would say, um, business ideas typically come from one of three P's."
  },
  {
   "s": 8.06,
   "e": 11.86,
   "text": "So it comes from a pain that you're currently experiencing, a past profession,"
  },
  {
   "s": 12.14,
   "e": 15.62,
   "text": "so the thing that you just quit or some of the jobs that you just quit, or passion."
  },
  {
   "s": 16.5,
   "e": 19.18,
   "text": "So something that you're inherently interested in that you would spend your time doing anyways."
  },
  {
   "s": 19.46,
   "e": 22.26,
   "text": "Some skill that you learned while you were in the workforce, which by the way is one"
  },
  {
   "s": 22.26,
   "e": 26.06,
   "text": "of the most proven ways of making money because the economy has already showed you that people"
  },
  {
   "s": 26.06,
   "e": 31.74,
   "text": "are willing to exchange money for that specific job. And so in the world of gig economies and"
  },
  {
   "s": 31.74,
   "e": 36.78,
   "text": "solopreneurs, every business can be dismantled into just jobs being done. And all of those"
  },
  {
   "s": 36.78,
   "e": 39.88,
   "text": "jobs can be fractionalized. You know, there's so many different components to a business,"
  },
  {
   "s": 40.3,
   "e": 42.24,
   "text": "you just need to learn one of them. And then it's like, boom,"
  },
  {
   "s": 42.24,
   "e": 46.14,
   "text": "you have a skill that you can trade for money that you don't have anybody else to report to."
  }
 ],
 "duration": 46.2
}